---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const L = site.legal;
const entity = L.entityName || '[Registered business name]';
const address = L.address || '[Registered address]';
const email = site.email || '[your@email]';
---
<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the evalkeen website and book a walkthrough with us."
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") apply to your use of this website and to walkthroughs and conversations you have
    with {entity} ("evalkeen", "we", "us"). By using this website, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree,
    please do not use the website.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What this website is for</h2>
  <p>
    This website describes the services we offer. It is for general information only. Nothing on it is an offer to
    provide services at a particular price or with a particular result.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Our services are covered by a separate agreement</h2>
  <p>
    If you decide to work with us, the scope, price, timelines, data handling and responsibilities will be set out in a
    written proposal or agreement that we both accept. If that agreement conflicts with these Terms, the agreement
    applies.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Free walkthroughs</h2>
  <p>
    Walkthroughs and initial consultations are free and carry no obligation for either side. Any suggestions we make
    during a walkthrough are general recommendations based on what you tell us. Either of us may decline to go further.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Demos, examples and results</h2>
  <p>
    Demo videos, sample flows and examples on this website are for illustration. Actual results depend on your
    business, your customers, your setup and other factors outside our control. We do not guarantee any specific
    number of leads, bookings, revenue or other outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>5. No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    We build software and automations. We do not provide medical, immigration, legal, tax or financial advice, and the
    assistants we build are designed not to give such advice. Decisions in those areas must be made by your qualified
    professionals.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Using this website</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the website for anything unlawful or fraudulent,</li>
    <li>try to break into, disrupt or overload the website or the systems behind it,</li>
    <li>copy, scrape or republish our content for commercial use without permission,</li>
    <li>pretend to be someone else when contacting us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The content of this website, including text, design, graphics, videos and the evalkeen name and logo, belongs to us
    or our licensors. You may view and share links to it, but you may not reuse it in other ways without our written
    permission. Ownership of anything we build for a client is set out in that client's agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Third-party services and links</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses and links to third-party services, such as YouTube, Loom, WhatsApp, booking tools and social media.
    We do not control them and are not responsible for their content, availability or privacy practices. Your use of
    them is governed by their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle personal data. It forms part of these Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    The website is provided "as is" and "as available". We try to keep it accurate and online, but we do not promise
    that it will always be available, error-free or up to date.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for any indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of profit,
    revenue, data or business opportunity, arising from your use of this website or from information on it. Our
    liability for paid services is set out in the agreement for those services. Nothing in these Terms limits liability
    that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of India. The courts at {L.courtsCity}, India, have exclusive jurisdiction over
    any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page, with its effective
    date at the top. Continuing to use the website after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>{entity}, {address}<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>
</LegalPage>
